ought is the primary documented federal-level hazard for the county.","All recorded federal disaster activity falls in the 1970s (1 event), with no subsequent declarations listed, suggesting limited recent federal disaster involvement but possible underrepresentation of more recent local or state-level impacts.","No clustering of multiple disasters in a short time span is evident; the single 1977 drought declaration does not indicate a recurring systemic vulnerability pattern in the available data.","Relative to the U.S. average (~1.5 federal declarations per county per year), Wayne County’s observed rate is slightly below average, supporting a moderate but not high federal disaster declaration frequency."],"sources":["OpenFEMA Disaster Declarations","US Census Bureau Geocoder"],"geojson":{"total":1,"county":"Wayne County","state":"","by_type":{"Drought":1},"by_decade":{"1970s":1},"year_range":[1977,1977],"notable":[{"number":"DR-3024","title":"DROUGHT","type":"Drought","date":"1977-01-20"}]},"threat_vector":null,"data_as_of":"2026-06-27 17:57 UTC","agent_skipped":false,"skip_reason":null}}},{"t":6543,"event":{"type":"risk_update","result":{"dimension":"wildfire","score":4,"level":"Very High","headline":"Very High wildfire threat driven by strong westerly winds and a fast-moving upwind fire ~77 km away.","details":["No active fire pixels are within 30 km, but a significant upwind fire with FRP 25.3 MW is located 77.4 km away and modeled to reach the site in approximately 5.6 hours at an estimated spread rate of 13.7 km/h, indicating a rapidly evolving threat (NASA FIRMS VIIRS NRT).","Strong westerly surface winds of 45.7 km/h with gusts to 60.8 km/h from 263° strongly favor eastward/downslope fire spread toward the location, increasing spotting distance and the likelihood of rapid fire growth and long-range ember transport.","Multiple low-FRP fire pixels (0.5–1.9 MW) detected 73–76 km away in the last 24 hours suggest a broader area of scattered fire activity or smoldering burns, reinforcing regional instability even though individual pixels are not intense (NASA FIRMS VIIRS NRT).","No named large-fire perimeters are reported within 100 miles, but the combination of strong winds, active upwind fire behavior, and typical early-summer dryness in this region means structural and vegetation fuels around the site are highly receptive to ignition and rapid spread (NIFC Active Fire Perimeters).","Given the projected arrival window of several hours and Very High threat level, pre-evacuation readiness, defensible space clearing, and close monitoring of official alerts are warranted, as conditions could escalate to Extreme if the upwind fire intensifies or spotting occurs ahead of the main front."],"sources":["NASA FIRMS VIIRS NRT","NIFC Active Fire Perimeters"],"geojson":null,"threat_vector":{"fire_lat":38.3866,"fire_lng":-112.3034,"distance_km":77.4,"frp_mw":25.3,"wind_speed_kmh":45.7,"wind_gusts_kmh":60.8,"wind_from_deg":263,"bearing_to_site_deg":97,"alignment_deg":14,"spread_rate_kmh":13.7,"est_hours":5.6},"data_as_of":"2026-06-27 17:57 UTC","agent_skipped":false,"skip_reason":null}}},{"t":6543,"event":{"type":"status","text":"Synthesizing assessment..."}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":"The"}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":" most"}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":" important"}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":" thing"}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":" to"}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":" know"}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":" right"}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":" now"}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":" is"}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":" that"}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":" Tor"}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":"rey"}},{"t":7114,"event":{"type":"briefing_token","text":" is"}},{"t":7114,"event